# HealthCare Operations & Revenue Optimization Dashboard

An end-to-end Power BI analytics solution designed to monitor clinical operations, evaluate revenue risk, and measure patient satisfaction across hospital departments and attending physicians.

---

## 📊 Dashboard Pages & Visual Architecture

### Page 1: Care Delivery & Operational Efficiency

Focuses on clinical throughput, treatment/medication cost drivers, and physician-level operational performance.

#### Key Performance Indicators (KPI Cards)
* **Average Length Of Stay (4.87 Days):** Measures average inpatient duration. Excludes outpatient encounters.
* **Total Bed Days (1,245 Days):** Total cumulative days spent by patients in inpatient care.
* **Emergency Visits (1,929):** Total volume of emergency department encounters.
* **Average Treatment Cost ($526.08):** Mean billing amount per visit across all stay types.
* **Clinical Overhead Cost ($109.21):** Mean medication and administrative clinical cost per visit.

#### Visual Breakdown
* **Revenue & Volume by Service Type (Horizontal Bar Chart):** Compares total gross revenue generated across Outpatient ($1.66M), Inpatient ($0.86M), and Emergency ($0.84M) service lines.
* **Revenue & Volume by Procedure (Stacked Horizontal Bar Chart):** Breaks down actual gross revenue versus pending uncollected revenue by clinical procedure (X-Ray, CT Scan, MRI Scan, Ultrasound, Blood Test).
* **Average Treatment & Medication Cost by Specialty (Clustered Column & Line Combo Chart):** Evaluates average treatment cost (columns) against average medication cost (line) across medical specialties (Neurology, Cardiology, Orthopedics, General Surgery, Pediatrics).
* **Doctor Operational Performance (Matrix Visual):** Detailed table profiling attending physicians across Total Visits, IPD count, EMR count, Treatment Billing, Medication Billing, Generated Revenue, and Uncollected Revenue %.

